    "title": "YWCA Alaska steps up as transportation needs grow after Typhoon Halong - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By La'shawn Donelson, Your Alaska Link ,\n6 hours ago Support is still being provided to people affected by Typhoon Halong, nearly two months after families were forced to evacuate their homes due to the storm’s impacts. City leaders in Anchorage say transportation has become the most urgent need. More than 600 evacuees have moved from hotels into semi-permanent housing, but some families are still staying in six hotels across the city. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
